<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n56531" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέλῡφος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εος</span>, τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sheath, case</i>, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> in fruits, <i>pod, shell</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>GA</u>
				752a20
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				2.4.2
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in
			animals, <i>sheath</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				510a28
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ κ. τῶν ᾠῶν</span>
			egg-<i>shells</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>GA</u>
				743a17
			</span></i>; in fish, <i>encasing membrane</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>HA</u>
				568b9
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ περὶ τὰς γενέσεις κ.</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				600b17
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>c.</b>
			<i>envelope</i>, of a chrysalis, ib.<i><span class="en">
				551a20
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				601a6
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>GA</u>
				758b17
			</span></i>; of the chrysalis of the stag-beetle, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>HA</u>
				551b19
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>d.</b>
			<i>shell</i> of crustaceous fish, ib. <i><span class="en">
				549b25
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>e.</b>
			<i>hollow</i> of the eye, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.439
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Crin.
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> metaph., of
			old dicasts, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντωμοσιῶν κελύφη</span>
			mere affidavit-<i>husks</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				545
			</span></i> (lyr.); of an old man's <i>boat</i>, which served as his
				<i>shell</i> or <i>coffin,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				AP
				9.242
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Antiphil.
			</span></i>). [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῡ</span>, exc. <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>C.</u>
				3.503
			</span></i>.] (Prob. cogn. with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καλύπτω</span>.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
